243 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The mechanical components of the 3D scanner were fabricated using a combination of laser cutting and Fused Deposition Modeling \(FDM\) 3D printing, chosen for their accessibility, precision, and cost-effectiveness. The base plate of the scanner, which serves as the foundation for the rotating platform and vertical guide system, was manufactured using laser cutting technology. The material selected was Wood All non-flat components, including the sensor holder, motor mounts, lead screw bracket, and platform disk, were fabricated using 3D printing \(FDM\). These parts were designed in CAD and printed using PLA)
/E (The mechanical components of the 3D scanner were fabricated using a combination of laser cutting and Fused Deposition Modeling \(FDM\) 3D printing, chosen for their accessibility, precision, and cost-effectiveness. The base plate of the scanner, which serves as the foundation for the rotating platform and vertical guide system, was manufactured using laser cutting technology. The material selected was Wood All non-flat components, including the sensor holder, motor mounts, lead screw bracket, and platform disk, were fabricated using 3D printing \(FDM\). These parts were designed in CAD and printed using PLA)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
